     "antwort_en": "Because a single figure shows nothing. The difference between the two positions is what reveals the circulatory reaction on changing position, and it is what explains the dizziness and makes the decision to stop demonstrable rather than an impression. And it is **an indication, not a proof**: a systematic orthostatic test is a different procedure and the doctor decides on it."
