     "antwort_en": "Because quality assurance is **a legal duty, not a voluntary initiative**, and because a near miss is **the cheapest opportunity to learn**: its cost is nil and its information is complete. And the gap that appeared tonight will catch somebody else next week — **and perhaps nobody will notice it**. And the report is not about the past but about the next time."
