     "antwort_en": "I report **the event and the conditions**, not the person: “a tablet from another patient's plan in the patient's cup, not administered; dispensed on a shift with one person for twelve patients; four-eyes check not documented”. **And the conditions are part of the report, not a footnote** — a report without conditions produces “pay more attention” and changes no process. And in most institutions the reporting system is non-punitive for exactly this reason."
