    "warum_en": "The most important thing in it is **two lines side by side**: what was actually done, and the actual duration. So the shortfall in personal care is not read as neglect, and the planned time is not read as the reality. **And the series of four figures is the evidence** that lifts the shortage later; the sentence “there is not enough time” does not do it. And the patient's worry is recorded **in her own words** rather than interpreted, and her consent to her son being informed is recorded — so that he is not rung behind her back.",
